steps.message:
The failing test confirms the missing seam. I’ll implement a global Stimulus formatter with five browser-side modes:

- adaptive default: clock today, “yesterday”/“tomorrow,” relative days within a week, then `Sep 12`;
- clock only;
- short date;
- weekday/date;
- full date/time.

The Rails helper will emit only a canonical UTC `<time>` and formatting metadata. I’ll then migrate the coherent set of interactive HTML views identified by the repository’s change metadata and add `local-time` to both page layouts so Turbo-inserted targets are formatted automatically.

